NVMemory media driver: a simple transfer engine (the N79's factory C: faulted the kernel)

The original split/head/tail bookkeeping counted alignment overhead across passes and faulted
("Illegal transfer operation!") on a write pattern the N79 factory user data layer produces at first boot;
every pass also read and wrote the client buffer at offset 0, so a transfer over 256 KB repeated its
first bytes. Now: one step = one sector-aligned window (at most KNVMemTransferBufferSize) at the current
position, client offset = bytes done; a partial head or tail sector of a write or format is read first
and merged; a short device transfer completes the request with KErrCorrupt.
--- a/baseport/syborg/mednvmemory/syborg_mednvmemory.cpp
+++ b/baseport/syborg/mednvmemory/syborg_mednvmemory.cpp
@@ -109,6 +109,14 @@
 	TUint32 iAlignmentOverhead;
 	TBool iReadModifyWrite;
 	TDfc iTransactionLaunchDfc;
+	// syborg-pg: the transfer engine (patches/qemu-baseport/0022): one step = one sector-aligned window of at
+	// most KNVMemTransferBufferSize bytes at iPos; a partial head or tail sector of a write/format is read first
+	void StartStep();
+	enum TPhase { EPhaseIdle, EPhaseRead, EPhaseRmwRead, EPhaseWrite };
+	TPhase iPhase;
+	TUint32 iStepHead;		// bytes of the first window sector before iPos
+	TUint32 iStepLen;		// client bytes in this step
+	TUint32 iStepSectors;	// window size in sectors
 	};
 
